I would tend to prefer the multipleGroup() function for vertical scaling as it's more flexible and parameters can be estimated concurrently, but yes sometimes you'll see very similar results in the single group implementation of the ideas. If it helps, the single group model is a special case of the multigroup model when the latent trait distributions are assumed to be the same and the item parameters are all constrained to be equal. Though you may be confused in some other aspect of the process that I don't quite see.

Phil

